# Personal financial data — never commit. Synthetic / documentation
# samples live in data/samples/ and are tracked.
data/*.json
data/*.moneydance
data/*.csv
data/*.ofx
data/*.qif
data/*.qfx

# Local environment
.env
.env.local
.env.*.local
*.env
# Database role passwords, as files (docker-compose `secrets:`). Real
# credentials — never committed. Generated by scripts/install.sh, or moved out
# of .env by scripts/migrate-db-secrets.sh.
#
# The glob covers a second install's directory too (secrets-g/ etc. for a
# parallel test stack). `secrets/` alone left those stageable, which is exactly
# the near-miss this pattern exists to prevent.
secrets/
secrets-*/
# The .env backups those scripts leave behind. These still contain the passwords
# that were moved out. Globbed, not named: `*.env` does not match
# `.env.pre-secrets`, and an exact `.env.pre-secrets` did not match a second
# stack's `g.env.pre-secrets` — each near-miss here is a live credential one
# `git add -A` away from being committed.
*.pre-secrets
.env.bak*

